4.1 Basic Definitions
A group (G, ∗) is a set with a binary operation satisfying three properties. The motivation for the definition reflected the behavior of (Z, +). Observe that Z also comes naturally equipped with multiplication ×. In the first lectures we collected some of the properties of (Z, +, ×). Motivated by this we make the following fundamental definition:
