(x + y) × z = x × z + y × z and x × (y + z) = x × y + x × z ∀x, y, z ∈ R
The identity for + is “zero”, denoted 0R (often just written as 0), and the identity for × is “one”, denoted 1R (often just written as 1).
Remarks. 1. To simplify the notation we will write x × y = xy for all x, y ∈ R.
2. Distributivity implies that we can “multiply” together finite sums:
