5.4 Solving Polynomials By Radicals
Suppose we wish to find the root of a polynomial f (x) = a0 + a1x + · · · + anxn ∈ Q[X]. If n = 2 we have the quadratic formula. It is natural to ask if there is a similar formula (in terms of the coefficients) for n > 2. It turns out that for n = 3 and n = 4 there are formulae,
